import pathlib,json,hashlib,re,datetime
p=pathlib.Path.cwd();prov=json.loads((p/'outputs/provenance.json').read_text());fetch=json.loads((p/'outputs/fetch-receipts.json').read_text());receipts={r['id']:r for r in fetch}
D={
371967:('KNOWN_SOURCE_THEOREM','Primary statement and main theorem plus exceptions read','The source main theorem characterizes all arc deletions and explicitly identifies exceptions. Strong tournaments avoid the displayed exceptions, so the reserved conjecture is covered by the source itself. The MathDB Fraisse–Thomassen quotation belongs to a different robustness conjecture, not its proof.','No new mechanism; no numerical search after source resolution.','None for discovery; source already claims the result.'),
362979:('PARKED_STRUCTURAL','Primary definitions, Table 1, Conjecture 1 and main results read','Source excludes trivial perfect codes by its coding-theoretic setting; a repetition/trivial-code endpoint correction is ineligible. The source proves many e=2 nonexistence cases and finiteness, not the full alphabet classification.','Sphere-packing divisibility for 13 non-prime-power alphabets, e=1,2, n from 2e+1 through 100; outputs/small-search.json. Divisibility does not construct codes.','A nontrivial perfect code over a non-prime-power alphabet or a full nonexistence theorem. Small parameter runs cannot certify the universal conjecture.'),
364090:('PARKED_STRUCTURAL','Primary definitions, cyclic-system theorem and Conjecture 4 read','The source theorem assumes noncontractible triangles in a cyclic system. Edge-width >=4 excludes those triangles, so its theorem does not settle this claim. The source critical-graph generation procedure and nearby results were inspected; running its catalogue procedure on a new entry would not earn discovery credit.','No new embedding/list-assignment enumeration implemented; exact topology and universal list assignments are substantial semantic costs.','A concrete toroidal embedding of edge-width >=4 with a failing five-list assignment, or a full structural proof.'),
365170:('PARKED_INFINITE_EXISTENCE','Primary construction and Conjecture 10 read','Theorem 1 and its tranquil hypergraph lemmas establish the m=1 case. The extension requires every used colour on every cycle to occur at least m+1 times. Finite unsuccessful searches cannot refute existence for arbitrary m,k.','No finite search claimed: reserved quantifiers demand an unbounded construction. Source Theorem 6 and Lemmas 7–9 were inspected for a short extension; none proved here.','A uniform replacement for bridgelessness in the auxiliary closed-walk construction that forces the higher multiplicity bound.'),
354344:('PARKED_PRIOR_PARTIAL','Primary Conjecture 1.6 and Section 6.3 proof bodies read','The source explicitly states its application proves the conjecture for sufficiently large groups. This does not by itself justify the MathDB all-orders solved label. Known 2-group results cover many small cases; no new all-orders solution claimed.','Exact zero-sum subset/partition searches for all 3/4/5-size multisets in 11 displayed abelian groups through order24; outputs/group-search.json. Larger requested sizes reduce by amalgamation, but the computation is still bounded.','Clear remaining finite mixed-order groups not covered by cited theorems and the source large-order threshold; do not count its own Lemma 6.25 as new.'),
355759:('PARKED_AFTER_SEARCH','Primary Conjecture 8 and multigraph interpretation read','A decomposition means every edge belongs to one colour class, with multiplicity1 or2 there; checking the stronger two-sum-on-all-edges convention would change the target. The source proves a different doubled-multigraph conjecture, not this one.','All connected labelled graphs of orders4 and5 (38+728); exact four-label edge assignment search until a witness. Every graph passed. outputs/graph-small-search.json.','A nonexistence certificate beyond known graph classes, or a full two-subgraph multiplicity construction.'),
350364:('PARKED_AFTER_SUSTAINED_SEARCH','Primary Conjectures 5.3/5.8, Theorem 5.2 and Proposition 5.9 proofs read','Source proves the exact transversal when every edge lies in equally many5-cycles, and shows its weighted max-cut conjecture would imply this claim. No new full-scope bridge found.','Seed156 random triangle-free cubic/edge-deleted subcubic graphs at orders8–60; exact one-edge-per-cycle backtracking. Also exhaustive first-neighbour-normalized triangle-free cubic order10; order12 capped prefix. See outputs/cycles-search.json and cubic-exact files for exact counts.','An unsatisfiable5-cycle edge-incidence system beyond the covered graphs, or a structural proof not already implicit in the source weighted machinery.'),
351455:('PARKED_AFTER_SEARCH','Primary truncated-distance, lattice-component definition, Conjecture9 and published Conjecture1.9 read','PTMC means perfect truncated-metric code, not the MathDB expanded total-multipacking phrase. Component-centred spheres and translation classes matter. Published2025 paper retains the nonexistence question.','All19^3=6859 homomorphisms from Z^3 to cyclic group19 tested on the singleton-centred truncated radius2 ball of size19. No tiling found. This excludes only this quotient/centre regime.','A lattice tiling by an allowed general component-centred truncated sphere, or a uniform lattice nonexistence theorem.'),
345350:('PARKED_AFTER_SEARCH','Primary conjecture and surrounding directed-cycle results read','Target permits antiparallel arcs, but each packed cycle must have at least3 vertices. A packing of digons does not resolve it.','All labelled loopless digraphs at orders3 and4; those with minimum in/out degree>=2 checked for a directed cycle of length>=3. Exact counts in outputs/small-search.json.','For k>=2 find a high-semidegree digraph with no k disjoint cycles of length>=3; no such witness or uniform packing proof obtained.'),
347519:('PARKED_STRUCTURAL','Primary Conjecture6.2 and adjacent intersection bounds read','Source proves intersection >=(8k-n+2)/5 and the full k=4 case. For k=5, its n/3 corollary already settles n<=15; those small instances cannot yield a new counterexample.','No redundant small graph search: the entire n<=15 range is source-covered. Longest-path semantic/certificate cost rises beyond that range.','A5-connected graph of order>=16 with two longest paths meeting in<=4 vertices, with maximum-length certification; or a full intersection proof.'),
348406:('EXCLUDED_SOURCE_INGREDIENT_CORRECTION','Primary Definitions3.1–3.3, Lemmas3.1–3.9, Proposition3.11/4.7, Conjecture4.8 and PDF versions read','The printed large-k optimiser conflicts with the source-own explicit Proposition3.11 construction and its claimed computational check through150. At k28, printed optimiser gives3347 while the source construction with seven of each100,010,001,111 gives3689. This is a source-ingredient bridge/printed inconsistency, not a new significant solution.','Polynomial independently generated from support-minimality; four tiny cases checked against direct complete codeword enumeration. Unit-transfer local searches at k151–180,200,250,500,1000,10000,1000000; corrected bit indexing preserved. outputs/codes-bridge.json and codes-search.json.','Do not count the printed refutation. The intended corrected global optimisation problem remains unproved; resolving it would require scope reconciliation first.'),
342671:('PARKED_INFINITE_PARAMETER','Primary hat-guessing definition and Conjecture1 read','Colouring number is degeneracy plus1, not chromatic number. A counterexample needs unbounded hat chromatic number at fixed colouring number; a single finite graph cannot refute existence of F.','No finite sweep presented as relevant certification. Later primary abstract leads retain an open degeneracy-bound problem, but no complete later-proof audit.','A uniform unbounded family at fixed degeneracy, or a uniform function bound.'),
402142:('PARKED_ASYMPTOTIC_FILTER_LEAK','Literal record and EMS landing page; related primary paper concluding section read','The statement contains Omega(m^(2/3)) despite reserve7 asymptotic filtering. A finite graph cannot contradict an unspecified positive asymptotic constant.','No finite sweep. Related author-hosted Hypergraph cuts above the average PDF retrieved; concluding section conjectures closing the5/9 to2/3 excess gap.','A uniform asymptotic bound, or an infinite family with excess o(m^(2/3)); EMS report body not retrieved.'),
364299:('PARKED_AFTER_SEARCH','Primary survey Conjecture4 and adjoining2-factor results read','Regular bipartite graphs do have spanning2-factors; empty-2-factor vacuity does not apply. Survey labels this a1980s Sheehan conjecture despite the newer metadata year.','46 seeded4-regular bipartite samples across side sizes4–10, generated as four edge-disjoint permutation matchings; each has a disconnected spanning2-factor. Counts include duplicates and are not an isomorphism census. outputs/graph-small-search.json.','A k>=4 regular bipartite graph all of whose2-factors are Hamiltonian, or a general disconnected2-factor theorem.'),
327034:('PARKED_AFTER_SEARCH','Primary digraph conventions and Conjecture4.2 read','Source setting has no directed cycles of length<=2; a symmetric complete planar digraph is not a legitimate endpoint counterexample.','Every orientation of K4 (64), octahedron (4096), wheel on6 vertices (1024), with exact acyclic subsets of required size. All passed. outputs/small-search.json.','A legitimate oriented planar graph with maximum induced acyclic set <3n/5, or a uniform planar-digraph theorem.'),
399000:('PARKED_ANALYTIC_FILTER_LEAK','Literal record, EMS landing page and related primary bibliographic leads','Rational matrices are essential. Known real/irrational finiteness counterexamples do not automatically refute the rational version. The target has an unbounded product-length quantifier and joint spectral radius; it is not a finite literal-certificate lead.','No bounded product sweep misrepresented as a finiteness refutation. Report proof body remains unread.','A rational matrix family with a proved absence of any spectrum-maximising finite product, or a uniform finiteness theorem.'),
326282:('PARKED_AFTER_SEARCH','Primary Conjecture1.7, neighbouring constant-colouring theorem and later primary restricted results read','MathDB reference falsely associates the Pawlik refutation of Scott general induced-subdivision conjecture with this K4 statement. The source explicitly separates them. The ISK4 four-colour question survives that quotation.','All labelled graphs on4,5,6 vertices (64,1024,32768), four-colouring then induced-subdivision checks on failures. No counterexample. outputs/graph-small-search.json.','A5-chromatic ISK4-free graph with complete induced-subdivision exclusion, or a uniform four-colouring theorem.2026 diamond-free result is restricted, not full scope.'),
373598:('HOLD_UNQUALIFIED_ORDINARY_COUNTEREXAMPLE','Full current primary HTML and definitions; cited obstruction only search-visible primary excerpts; publication retention unverified','An18-vertex r5 split graph passes literal hypotheses and is not Hamilton-connected. Complete ordinary proof and explicit edge list supplied in CASE-373598.md. Full companion-construction comparison and positive published-version retention remain material gaps. No novelty or significance acceptance and no Lean endpoint.','All cyclic5-subsets for side sizes7–12; selected n9 block. All4048 deletions of<=4 vertices, all15444 centre/six-neighbour-subset forbidden checks. outputs/split-search.json.','Before Lean investment, root must clear source-publication retention, source/companion augmentation and classical balanced-split boundary objections. Then certify literal vertex connectivity, induced graph exclusions and Hamiltonian-path independent-set obstruction.'),
361120:('PARKED_GEOMETRIC_SEMANTICS','Primary definitions, construction families and concluding Conjecture1 read; published statement visible via primary index','Fully leafed means globally leaf-optimal induced subtree of a Penrose P2 tiling, not an arbitrary abstract subcubic tree. A counterexample needs both realizability in the tiling and global optimality. Existing caterpillars and appendix grafting are the source machinery.','No validated Penrose patch enumerator implemented; abstract-tree enumeration would not establish source scope. Published DMTCS2025 record retains the same concluding conjecture.','A tile-realised optimal noncaterpillar saturated tree, or a non-saturated optimal tree without the required graft decomposition, with literal geometric semantics.'),
338977:('KNOWN_PUBLIC_RESOLUTION','Original Conjecture7.5 and later primary Theorem1.2 plus explanatory comparison read','Brettell–Semple–Toft arXiv2409.13834 explicitly says Theorem1.2 resolves original Conjecture7.5 and lists missing exceptional matroids. The original classification was incomplete.','No rediscovery search after direct primary resolution. Later full theorem and family definitions are cached in sources/matroids-new.html.','None for discovery; mathematical work is already public.')}
res={}
for i in json.loads((p/'reservation.json').read_text())['ids']:
 q=prov[str(i)];r=q['record'];status,depth,finding,attempt,gap=D[i];statement=r['statement'];ab=p/'sources'/f'{i}-abs.txt';meta=ab.read_text() if ab.exists() else ''
 versions=re.findall(r'\[v\d+\][^\n]*',meta)
 res[str(i)]={'mathdb_id':i,'title':r['title'],'outcome':status,'discovery_count_credit':0,'root_acceptance':'not requested or claimed; root decides','review_depth':depth,'literal_statement':statement,'statement_sha256':hashlib.sha256(statement.encode()).hexdigest(),'provenance':{k:v for k,v in q.items() if k!='record'},'raw_file':f'raw/{i}.jsonl','primary_receipt':receipts[i],'current_version_metadata_file':f'sources/{i}-abs.html' if ab.exists() else None,'version_history_visible':versions,'historical_screen':'outputs/historical-exact-id-hits.txt: no exact ID hits in prior batch Markdown; index absence is not global novelty','finding':finding,'attempts_and_exact_coverage':attempt,'remaining_gap':gap,'formal_status':'No Lean endpoint; no formal proof or acceptance claimed','limitations':'Bounded review only. No worldwide novelty clearance. Parked entries have not had every cited proof or every historical arXiv version read.'}
assert len(res)==20 and set(map(int,res))==set(json.loads((p/'reservation.json').read_text())['ids'])
(p/'results.json').write_text(json.dumps(res,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
print('wrote',len(res),'ID-keyed results')
